Falsifies `jh7110_clock_and_reset::verification::clock_divider_is_the_low_24_bits_and_nothing_else`.

The defect: the divider mask is one bit too wide, so bit 24, the lowest bit of the mux field,
reads as part of the divider.

Expected to fail: the harness's first assertion, equality with the word's low 24 bits.

diff --git a/crates/jh7110_clock_and_reset/src/lib.rs b/crates/jh7110_clock_and_reset/src/lib.rs
index 7cc680a83..0e74ddbcc 100644
--- a/crates/jh7110_clock_and_reset/src/lib.rs
+++ b/crates/jh7110_clock_and_reset/src/lib.rs
@@ -426,7 +426,7 @@ pub const SDIO_BRING_UP: [&[Step]; 2] = [
 /// Name: ratified 2026-10-26 (UTC).
 #[must_use]
 pub const fn clock_divider(word: u32) -> u32 {
-    word & 0x00ff_ffff
+    word & 0x01ff_ffff
 }
 
